  "question": {
    ":question/id": "8fb01b37-cc09-59fe-ad0f-24d528334d07",
    ":question/problem": "Find $AB$, if \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -10\\end{bmatrix}.$",
    ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 7 & 1\\cdot (-10) \\\\ (-4)\\cdot 7 & (-4)\\cdot (-10) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 7 & (-2)\\cdot (-10)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -10 \\\\ -28 & 40 \\\\ -14 & 20\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
